BLD-01: five libScotch sources missing from the CMake build (+ one dead file compiled in).

1. Text check (ships as ci/check_sources.sh in patch 0005; the copy here is the first version):
     sh ci/check_sources.sh $WORK/src-base/src
   pristine output:
     libscotch: source lists differ ('<': Makefile only, '>': CMake only)
     > common_error.c
     < hgraph_dump.c
     < library_context_mesh.c
     < library_context_mesh_f.c
     < library_graph_induce_f.c
     < library_memory_f.c
     libesmumps: source lists differ ('<': Makefile only, '>': CMake only)
     > symbol_fax.c
     rc=1
   patched: no output, rc=0.

2. Symbols of the CMake-built library:
     nm -D $WORK/cm/base32/lib/libscotch.so | grep -E ' T (SCOTCH_contextBindMesh|SCOTCHFCONTEXTBINDMESH|scotchfgraphinducelist_|scotchfgraphinducepart_|scotchfnumsizeof_|_SCOTCHhgraphDump|errorPrint)$'
   pristine: only "T errorPrint" (see PS2-G29-1); none of the six expected symbols.
   patched ($WORK/cm/patched32/lib/libscotch.so):
     T SCOTCHFCONTEXTBINDMESH
     T SCOTCH_contextBindMesh
     T _SCOTCHhgraphDump
     T scotchfgraphinducelist_
     T scotchfgraphinducepart_
     T scotchfnumsizeof_
   Makefile-built reference (INFRA/asan/lib/libscotch.so) has all six.
   Note: "scotchfmemcur" (first pass's evidence) comes from library_common_f.c, which CMake
   always built; the wrapper that library_memory_f.c provides is "scotchfnumsizeof".
